<title>JAPAN: Japan Nov domestic vehicle sales up 14.0% yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Japan Nov domestic vehicle sales up 14.0% yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-12-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's domestic vehicle sales rose 14.0 percent from a year earlier to 507,548 units in November, the Japan Automobile Dealers' Association said on Monday.</p>
<p>The November sales breakdown was as follows (with percentage changes from a year earlier):</p>
<p> Total cars		355,261  up   15.6 percent</p>
<p> - Cars over 2000 cc    94,228  up   17.2 percent</p>
<p> - Cars under 2000 cc  261,033  up   15.0 percent</p>
<p> Trucks		    151,331  up   10.5 percent</p>
<p> - Heavy trucks	   12,243  up   20.5 percent</p>
<p> - Light trucks	  139,088  up    9.7 percent</p>
<p> Buses			   956  up    8.1 percent</p>
<p>November sales included 35,933 imported vehicles, up 4.1 percent from the year before.</p>
<p>November vehicle sales by five major Japanese makers were as follows (with percentage changes from a year earlier):</p>
<p> Toyota Motor     229,598  up   19.2 percent</p>
<p> Nissan Motor	90,607  up    0.3 percent</p>
<p> Honda Motor	 53,497  up   47.6 percent</p>
<p> Mitsubishi Motors 38,249  up    0.2 percent</p>
<p> Mazda Motor	 25,114  up    0.4 percent</p>
